<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mississippi Band of Choctaw Indians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> Band of Choctaw Indians is a federally recognised Native American nation in east-central Mississippi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, formed by descendants of Choctaw who stayed in their homeland after the removals of the 1830s. Left landless and marginalised for decades, they regained federal recognition in 1945 and hold a reservation centred on Pearl River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, Mississippi.</p></div>
